<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Bancomer started.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Bancomer started.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- J.P. Morgan said analyst Brian Pearl started coverage of Mexico's Banco Financiero Bancomer on Wednesday with a rating of market underperformer.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Bancomer should suffer a sharp decline in earnings before provisions and taxes (EBPT) over the next several years,&quot; Pearl wrote in a report.</p>
<p>-- &quot;... This decline in expected EBPT is a result of year-over-year compression in net interest margin ... from six percent in 1996 to 4.1 percent in 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's B shares were off 0.10 peso to 2.83 pesos in Mexico City.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
